    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27486" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">măcĭo</span></b> ,
		āre, v. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make lean, thin</i>, or <i>meagre, to
			reduce</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caspii maris fauces mirum in modum maciantur
					imbribus, crescunt aestibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 15, 18</span></i>
			; cf.: macio <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διακναίω</span>, Gloss.
			Philox.</div>
